* fits comfortably within the **11.0-minute target**, leaving ample reserve to finish **all 20 questions** without panic.", "margin_discipline": "QCAB Compliant (Margins Respected)", "total_pages": 2}, "syllabus_mapping": {"paper": "GS1", "paper_display": "GS-1 (Modern Indian History & Freedom Struggle)", "discipline": "Modern Indian History & National Movement", "micro_topic": "Significant Events, Personalities & Issues of the Freedom Struggle", "pyq_trend_frequency": "Standard UPSC Mains Notification Theme \u2022 High-Yield Revision Pillar", "directive": "Discuss", "directive_guidance": "Wide multi-dimensional coverage with clear thematic sub-headings."}, "micro_marking_arithmetic": {"formula_display": "Intro (1.0/2.0) + Core (3.0/7.0) + Value (0.5/2.5) + Pres (0.5/1.5) + Conc (1.5/2.0) = 6.5 / 15.0", "intro_score": 1.0, "intro_max": 2.0, "core_demand_score": 3.0, "core_demand_max": 7.0, "value_add_score": 0.5, "value_add_max": 2.5, "presentation_score": 0.5, "presentation_max": 1.5, "conclusion_score": 1.5, "conclusion_max": 2.0, "total_score": 6.5, "max_marks": 15, "is_mathematically_verified": true}, "keyword_toolkit_title": "Historical Sources, Economic Doctrines & Historiographical Concepts", "missing_keywords_cards": [{"number": 1, "term": "Drain of Wealth", "thinker": "Dadabhai Naoroji''s Economic Critique", "domain_or_thinker": "\u26a1 Shallow Mention \u2014 Analytical Upgrade Needed", "definition": "You cited **Drain of Wealth** in passing\u2014substantiate its core analytical application: The systematic transfer of Indian capital and surplus revenue to Britain without economic returns, initiated post-Plassey.", "where_to_use": "Build directly on your existing Drain of Wealth point on your answer sheet.", "how_to_use_one_line": "Anchor under **Drain of Wealth**: ''...initiating a unilateral transfer of Indian tribute that starved domestic capital formation.''"}, {"number": 2, "term": "Diplomatic Revolution of 1756", "thinker": "Global Seven Years'' War Context", "domain_or_thinker": "Global Geopolitics", "definition": "The European realignment that linked the Anglo-French rivalry in Bengal directly to worldwide imperial supremacy.", "where_to_use": "Page 3 \u2022 Inside your ''Worldwide manoeuvre of British'' section", "how_to_use_one_line": "Cite **Diplomatic Revolution of 1756**: ''...subordinating Indian territorial revenues to finance Britain''s global military hegemony against France.''"}, {"number": 3, "term": "Military Fiscal State", "thinker": "Bayly''s Historiographical Model", "domain_or_thinker": "State Formation Theory", "definition": "A state that extracts massive agrarian surplus through centralized revenue extraction to fund expansionist warfare.", "where_to_use": "Page 1 \u2022 Beside your ''Won be treasury, not military prowess'' boxed point", "how_to_use_one_line": "Substantiate via **Military Fiscal State**: ''...transforming the EIC into a formidable military-fiscal apparatus anchored in Bengal''s treasury.''"}, {"number": 4, "term": "Diwani Rights of 1765", "thinker": "Constitutional Transition Milestone", "domain_or_thinker": "Administrative Evolution", "definition": "The formal acquisition of revenue collection rights in Bengal, Bihar, and Odisha that legitimized company rule.", "where_to_use": "Final Page \u2022 Attach to the end of your closing ''Framed context for battle of Buxar'' point", "how_to_use_one_line": "Recommend via **Diwani Rights of 1765**: Institutionalized indirect political suzerainty before culminating in outright annexation."}], "micro_hygiene": {"spelling_errors": ["uddaualal (Siraj-ud-daulah)", "guzzlers (revenue extractors)"], "grammar_and_syntax": "Phrasing is mostly expressive, though some sentences rely on informal terms like ''money guzzlers''.", "presentation_and_word_count": "Good use of vertical space, flowcharts, and structured numbering."}, "directive_compliance": {"directive": "Discuss", "adherence_score": "8/10", "evaluation": "Successfully explored both domestic Indian impacts and broader global mercantilist shifts.", "gap": "Lacked specific European geopolitical linkages such as the Seven Years'' War."}, "rubric_scores": {"intro_score": 1.0, "intro_max": 2.0, "core_demand_score": 3.0, "core_demand_max": 7.0, "value_add_score": 0.5, "value_add_max": 2.5, "presentation_score": 0.5, "presentation_max": 1.5, "conclusion_score": 1.5, "conclusion_max": 2.0}, "sub_part_step_marking": [{"step_label": "1. Introduction (Context & Baseline Hook)", "sub_heading": "Significance of Plassey in Indian and Global History", "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "awarded": 1.0, "max": 2.0, "quoted_written": "\u2713 Solid premise established by framing Plassey as the foundation of British imperial prowess."}, {"step_label": "2. Part A \u2014 Impact on Indian Course", "sub_heading": "Domestic Political, Economic, and Military Repercussions", "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "awarded": 1.5, "max": 4.25, "quoted_written": "\u2713 Well-structured flowchart on treasury capture, puppet rule, and exploitation of social cleavages."}, {"step_label": "3. Part B \u2014 Global & World Historical Impact", "sub_heading": "Worldwide Manoeuvres and Mercantilist Expansion", "demand_status": "Partially Fulfilled", "awarded": 1.25, "max": 4.25, "quoted_written": "\u26a0\ufe0f Covered trader-to-ruler transition; lacked explicit connection to European colonial rivalries."}, {"step_label": "4. Part C \u2014 Conclusion (Closing Synthesis)", "sub_heading": "Synthesizing Imperialist Push and Drain of Wealth", "demand_status": "Partially Fulfilled", "awarded": 1.25, "max": 2.5, "quoted_written": "\u2713 **Closing Synthesis Evaluated**: Effectively summarizes the multidimensional colonial extraction, though slightly dense in terminology.", "step_up_lever": "Synthesizing **epigraphical and archival evidence** with **living cultural continuity** ensures that India''s rich civilizational heritage continues to nurture national identity and constitutional fraternity."}, {"step_label": "5. Presentation & Structure", "sub_heading": "Flowcharts, Boxed Headings, and Legibility", "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "awarded": 1.5, "max": 2.0, "quoted_written": "\u2713 Excellent visual organization with clear hierarchical flowcharts."}], "subpart_marks_breakdown": [{"part_name": "1. Introduction (Context & Baseline Hook)", "max_marks": 2.0, "marks_awarded": 1.0, "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "analysis": "Significance of Plassey in Indian and Global History", "scoring_rationale": "\u2713 Solid premise established by framing Plassey as the foundation of British imperial prowess."}, {"part_name": "2. Part A \u2014 Impact on Indian Course", "max_marks": 4.25, "marks_awarded": 1.5, "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "analysis": "Domestic Political, Economic, and Military Repercussions", "scoring_rationale": "\u2713 Well-structured flowchart on treasury capture, puppet rule, and exploitation of social cleavages."}, {"part_name": "3. Part B \u2014 Global & World Historical Impact", "max_marks": 4.25, "marks_awarded": 1.25, "demand_status": "Partially Fulfilled", "analysis": "Worldwide Manoeuvres and Mercantilist Expansion", "scoring_rationale": "\u26a0\ufe0f Covered trader-to-ruler transition; lacked explicit connection to European colonial rivalries."}, {"part_name": "4. Part C \u2014 Conclusion (Closing Synthesis)", "max_marks": 2.5, "marks_awarded": 1.25, "demand_status": "Partially Fulfilled", "analysis": "Synthesizing Imperialist Push and Drain of Wealth", "scoring_rationale": "\u2713 **Closing Synthesis Evaluated**: Effectively summarizes the multidimensional colonial extraction, though slightly dense in terminology."}, {"part_name": "5. Presentation & Structure", "max_marks": 2.0, "marks_awarded": 1.5, "demand_status": "Demand Fulfilled", "analysis": "Flowcharts, Boxed Headings, and Legibility", "scoring_rationale": "\u2713 Excellent visual organization with clear hierarchical flowcharts."}], "point_by_point_audit": [{"page": 1, "badge": "Page 1 \u2022 Flowchart & Opening", "title": "Battle of Plassey (1757) Structural Flowchart", "what_you_wrote": "Battle of Plassey -> Siraj-ud-daulah & others -> Bengal -> Won by treasury, not military prowess", "examiner_verdict": "Effective visual representation of how political conspiracy substituted for military strength.", "credit_badge": "\u2713 +1.50M Rewarded", "is_positive": true}, {"page": 2, "badge": "Page 2 \u2022 Numbered Points 1 to 4", "title": "Impact on Course in India", "what_you_wrote": "Exploitation of social cleavage... Taste of imperial power... Private trade... Framed context for Buxar", "examiner_verdict": "Good analytical progression from divide-and-rule to mercantile greed and the road to Buxar.", "credit_badge": "\u2713 +1.50M Credit", "is_positive": true}, {"page": 3, "badge": "Page 3 \u2022 Global Manoeuvres", "title": "Worldwide Manoeuvring of British", "what_you_wrote": "Traders to rulers across colonies... Mercantilism furthered by capture of power... Forceful conquerorship", "examiner_verdict": "Broadened the scope beyond India, though specific global comparative examples would enhance depth.", "credit_badge": "\u2794 +1.00M Scope", "is_positive": true}, {"page": 3, "badge": "Page 3 \u2022 Conclusion", "title": "Ergo, British victory in Plassey...", "what_you_wrote": "Ergo, British victory in Plassey heralded an imperialist push that aided colonialism of Indian mind, man, material and money...", "examiner_verdict": "Encompasses multi-dimensional drain, but phrasing is slightly repetitive.", "credit_badge": "\u2713 +0.50M Credit", "is_positive": true}], "intro_audit": {"intro_archetype": "Historical / Evolutionary", "topic_vs_question_relevance": "Directly targets the foundational turning point of 1757 as a global watershed.", "current_critique": "The opening sentence clearly articulates the transition from commercial enterprise to imperial paramountcy.", "is_circular_intro": false, "missing_elements": [], "model_intro_rewrite": "The Battle of Plassey (1757) was a watershed moment that transformed the East India Company from a commercial trading corporation into a territorial power, fundamentally altering Asian trade and global imperial dynamics."}, "body_audit": {"overall_assessment": "The body is exceptionally well-structured with clear subheadings, numbered analytical points, and effective flowchart mapping on Page 1. It successfully traces the dual domestic and global implications of the conflict.", "strengths": ["**Visual Structuring (Page 1)**: Excellent flowchart mapping the causes and immediate outcomes of Plassey, highlighting financial conquest over pure military prowess. Your structured presentation of this dimension demonstrated strong conceptual grasp, fulfilling examiner expectations and securing primary demand marks.", "**Multidimensional Impact (Page 2)**: You clearly articulated this on your sheet by citing **Exploitation of social cleavage... Taste of imperial power... Private trade... Framed context for Buxar**. Systematic breakdown of social cleavages, private trade abuse, and the systematic setting of precedence for Buxar. This demonstrated clear conceptual grounding and secured core demand marks.", "**Global Perspective (Page 3)**: Extension of the argument from regional conquest in Bengal to worldwide mercantilist maneuvering and colonial expansion. Your structured presentation of this dimension demonstrated strong conceptual grasp, fulfilling examiner expectations and securing primary demand marks.", "**Historiographical Flow (Page 2-3)**: Clear conceptual progression from commercial monopoly to administrative paramountcy. Your structured presentation of this dimension demonstrated strong conceptual grasp, fulfilling examiner expectations and securing primary demand marks."], "critical_gaps": ["**Geopolitical Linkage (Page 3)**: Failed to explicitly mention the contemporary Seven Years'' War (1756\u201363) which linked European rivalries directly to Indian conquests.", "**Economic Mechanism (Page 2)**: Did not detail the exact mechanics of dastaks misuse and how it destroyed native merchant competition."], "missing_dimensions": ["**European Geopolitical Context**: The linkage between Anglo-French rivalry in Europe and India.", "**Native Economic Impact**: The collapse of indigenous banking houses like Jagat Seths post-Plassey."]}, "value_add_checklist": {"category_1": {"title": "Global Conventions, Frameworks & Policies", "items": [{"item": "Mercantilist Bullion Drain & Global Capital Accumulation", "where_to_write": "Page 3, under ''Mercantilism furthered by capture of power''", "how_to_write": "Connect Bengal plunder directly to financing the British Industrial Revolution."}]}, "category_2": {"title": "Scientific Theories, Judicial Verdicts & Doctrines", "items": [{"item": "Military-Fiscal State Paradigm (C.A. Bayly)", "where_to_write": "Page 1, beside treasury vs military prowess flowchart", "how_to_write": "Cite Bayly''s model to explain how revenue extraction funded subsequent military expansion."}]}, "category_3": {"title": "Empirical Data, Case Studies & Real-World Flashpoints", "items": [{"item": "Mir Jafar''s Tribute of over 2 Million Pounds", "where_to_write": "Page 2, under ''revenue guzzlers'' point", "how_to_write": "Mention the massive personal fortunes and company reparations extracted from Bengal''s treasury."}]}, "category_4": {"title": "Recommended Exam-Hall Micro-Diagram / Map", "items": [{"item": "Trilateral Flow of Wealth (Bengal -> London -> Global Markets)", "where_to_write": "Page 3 margin micro-box", "how_to_write": "Draw a 3-node arrow diagram illustrating export financing via Indian territorial revenue."}]}}, "recommended_diagram_visual": "[Plassey 1757: Treasury Capture] \u2500\u2500\u2794 [Diwani 1765: Revenue Extraction] \u2500\u2500\u2794 [Industrial Revolution Financing]", "conclusion_audit": {"conclusion_archetype": "Historical-Significance", "failure_mode": "None (Well-synthesized)", "current_critique": "\u2713 **Closing Synthesis Evaluated**: Effectively summarizes the multidimensional colonial extraction, though slightly dense in terminology.", "aligns_with_national_goals": true, "model_conclusion_rewrite": "Thus, Plassey was not merely a regional victory in Bengal, but the institutional genesis of British global hegemony, shifting the trajectory of modern world history.", "is_unwritten": false, "score": 1.5}, "case_study_audit": {"is_case_study": false, "protagonist_role": "", "core_ethical_conflict": "", "candidate_decision_evaluation": {"chosen_course_of_action": "", "character_and_intent_assessment": "", "is_mark_reducing_decision": false, "mark_reduction_risk_reason": ""}, "best_alternative_course_of_action": {"strategy_title": "", "phase_1_immediate": "", "phase_2_procedural": "", "phase_3_systemic": ""}, "options_matrix": []}, "transcribed_text": "[Page 1] Battle of Plassey (1757) laid the foundation for march of British, from Imperialism to colonial prowess. Siraj-uddaual and others -> Battle of Plassey -> Won be treasury, not military prowess. A decidedly factor for British rights and puppeteering. Impact on course in India: 1) Laid foundation stone of white man on Indian soil. 2) Deeper understanding of faultlines of India, exploited severely over course of time. 2) Battle of Buxar with military readiness.\n[Page 2] 3) Exploitation of social cleavage and differences in Plassey lead to mastering of ''divide and rule''. 4) Taste of imperial power to the company increased greed -> private trade, revenue guzzlers, rights over respectful pleading. 5) Framed context for battle of Buxar, the final blow to Bengal''s plight. 6) Mercantilism aided by provision of ''men, material, money'', as gained post Plassey. 7) Military acumen of Indians gauged, used it to tailor own self to better the Indians hereafter.\n[Page 3] In addition to impact on Indian history, it aided worldwide manoeuvring of British: 1) Traders to rulers across colonies. 2) Mercantilism furthered by capture of power. 3) Forceful conquerorship and safeguarding of financial interest -> fortification. 4) Establishment of dense networks of intelligence within regimes -> Mughal breakdown. 5) Crushing revolts with force and farce -> Revolt of 1857, Doctrine of Lapse, Paramountcy. Ergo, British victory in Plassey heralded an imperialist push that aided colonialism of Indian mind, man, material and money - from ''Drain of wealth'' to ''Brain drain'' caused by colonisation of mind.", "full_model_answer": "The Battle of Plassey (1757) was a watershed moment that transformed the East India Company from a commercial trading corporation into a de facto territorial power, fundamentally altering Asian trade and global imperial dynamics.\n\nDomestically in India, Plassey established the paradigm of indirect rule through puppets, replacing sovereign resistance with financial subjugation. As C.A. Bayly notes, it enabled the creation of a ''military-fiscal state'' where Bengal''s vast agrarian surplus funded subsequent military expansion across the subcontinent. It exposed indigenous political fragmentation, perfecting the doctrine of divide-and-rule and setting the stage for the decisive Battle of Buxar (1764).\n\nGlobally, Plassey financed Britain''s mercantilist expansion and its worldwide struggle against France during the Seven Years'' War. The unhindered inflow of Indian bullion and tribute provided crucial capital accumulation that lubricated the early phases of the British Industrial Revolution, establishing a blueprint for corporate imperialism across global colonies.\n\nThus, Plassey was not merely a regional victory in Bengal, but the institutional genesis of British global hegemony, shifting the trajectory of modern world history.", "jargon_buster": [{"term": "Military-Fiscal State", "meaning": "A state that uses centralized taxation and financial extraction to fund large military apparatuses for expansion."}, {"term": "Mercantilism", "meaning": "An economic doctrine where state power is maximized through the restriction of colonial trade and extraction of wealth."}], "rewrite_verification": {"is_same_question_topic": true, "mismatch_reason": "", "is_identical_copy": false, "improvements_detected": true, "improvement_summary": "Candidate successfully covered both domestic political impacts and broader global mercantile shifts."}, "current_affairs_value_add": {"current_example_insertion": {"paragraph_target": "Page 3 \u2022 Under your ''Worldwide manoeuvre of British'' section", "current_weakness": "Lacked specific historiographical or global geopolitical context.", "recommended_insertion": "Integrate the Seven Years'' War (1756\u20131763) as the global canvas against which Plassey secured British naval and commercial supremacy.", "marks_gain": "+0.5 to +1.0 Mark"}, "current_examples": [{"example_title": "Seven Years'' War Nexus", "paragraph_target": "Page 3 \u2022 Beside your global maneuvering points", "recommended_insertion": "Connect Bengal''s financial surplus directly to funding British naval operations against French fleets globally.", "marks_gain": "+0.5 Mark"}], "high_yield_data_reports": ["C.A. Bayly''s ''Indian Society and the Making of the British Empire''", "Dadabhai Naoroji''s Drain of Wealth theory"], "diagram_recommendation": {"relevance_verdict": "HIGH_ROI", "space_utilization_advice": "The flowchart on Page 1 is well done; maintain similar concise structural schematics.", "concept_title": "Global Imperial Convergence Schematic", "structure": "Bengal Treasury Capture \u2500\u2500\u2794 Industrial Financing in Britain \u2500\u2500\u2794 Global Hegemony over France", "exam_hall_sketch_tip": "Keep arrow chains compact and neat."}}, "visual_annotations": [{"page": 1, "approx_y_percent": 33, "start_y_percent": 24.0, "end_y_percent": 42.0, "tag": "Intro: Context & Conceptual Definition", "type": "tick", "marks_awarded": "+1.0 / 2.0", "remark": "\u2713 **Direct Premise**: Opened directly with *\"Battle of Plassey (1757) laid the foundation for march of British\"*, framing the core thesis effectively.\n\u270e **Opening Upgrade**: Add reference to the transition from merchant capital to territorial sovereignty.", "score": 1.0, "max": 2.0}, {"page": 1, "approx_y_percent": 66, "start_y_percent": 44.0, "end_y_percent": 88.0, "tag": "Body: Impact on Course in India", "type": "tick", "marks_awarded": "+1.5 / 3.5", "remark": "\u2713 **Core Argumentation**: Articulated *\"Won be treasury, not military prowess\"* using a clear structural flowchart.\n\u270e **Substantive Elevation**: Explicitly mention the acquisition of Diwani rights (1765) as the logical culmination.", "score": 1.5, "max": 3.5}, {"page": 2, "approx_y_percent": 50, "start_y_percent": 12.0, "end_y_percent": 88.0, "tag": "Body: Core Analysis (Point 3)", "type": "tick", "marks_awarded": "+1.5 / 3.5", "remark": "\u2713 **Analytical Dimension**: Examined *\"Traders to rulers across colonies\"* and mercantilist expansion.\n\u270e **Substantive Elevation**: Connect corporate militarism to the Seven Years'' War and European geopolitical rivalries.", "score": 1.5, "max": 4.0}, {"page": 3, "tag": "Body: Core Demand", "start_y_percent": 10.0, "end_y_percent": 68.0, "approx_y_percent": 39, "type": "tick", "marks_awarded": "+1.0 / 4.0", "remark": "\u2713 **Worldwide Manoeuvring of British**: Broadened the scope beyond India, though specific global comparative examples would enhance depth.\n\u2713 **Ergo, British victory in Plassey...**: Encompasses multi-dimensional drain, but phrasing is slightly repetitive.", "score": 1.0, "max": 3.0}, {"page": 3, "approx_y_percent": 74, "start_y_percent": 70.0, "end_y_percent": 78.0, "tag": "Conclusion", "type": "warning", "marks_awarded": "+1.5 / 2.0", "remark": "\u2713 **Closing Synthesis Evaluated**: Effectively summarizes the multidimensional colonial extraction, though slightly dense in terminology.\n\u270e **To Score Full Marks**: Synthesizing **epigraphical and archival evidence** with **living cultural continuity** ensures that India''s rich civilizational heritage continues to nurture national identity and constitutional fraternity.", "score": 1.5, "max": 2.5}], "is_hindi": false, "medium": "english", "model_answer_meta": {"is_adaptive": true, "word_count": 170, "target_words": 250, "point_count": 0, "badge_text": "\u2728 Topper Synthesis (Candidate Points Retained + High-Yield Dimensions)", "badge_text_hindi": "\u2728 \u0905\u092d\u094d\u092f\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0940-\u0938\u0902\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0927\u093f\u0924 \u092e\u0949\u0921\u0932 \u0909\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0930 (\u092e\u093e\u0928\u094d\u092f \u092c\u093f\u0902\u0926\u0941 \u0938\u0941\u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093f\u0924 + \u092a\u0930\u0940\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u092e\u0942\u0932\u094d\u092f-\u0938\u0902\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0927\u0928)"}, "examiner_overall_verdict": "Strong historical structuring with excellent use of headings and conceptual flowcharts. However, it lacks specific historiographical references and broader global geopolitical linkages.", "detected_paper_display": "GS-1 (Modern Indian History & Freedom Struggle)", "subject_discipline": "Modern Indian History & National Movement", "syllabus_subheading": "Significant Events, Personalities & Issues of the Freedom Struggle", "is_incomplete_answer": false, "is_candidate_incomplete_answer": false, "_meta_visual_hashes": ["808ca69e66a48cc8", "84e6b6b8c080a498", "94c2d678e6a05059"], "_meta_eval_id": "eval_1792074642_224d41", "_meta_created_at": "2026-10-15 14:30:42", "created_at": "2026-10-15 14:30:42", "evaluated_at": "2026-10-15 14:30:42", "_meta_user_email": "shivram@gmail.com", "_meta_paper": "GS1", "_meta_max_marks": 15, "_meta_is_rewrite": 0, "_meta_baseline_eval_id": null, "_meta_file_hash": "7b31c2de212e2ebed5e6565516cfbfe275b2d0e19c55430ba54c0eae951bd18a", "_meta_thumbnail": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "_meta_pages": ["data:image/jpeg;base64,", "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "data:image/jpeg;base64,"]}', '